# check_indeterminate_handling.sh baseline
# Pre-existing findings, accepted so the checker can block NEW ones.
# Entries are <repo-relative-path><TAB><finding-type>. Line numbers are
# deliberately excluded so edits elsewhere in a file do not resurrect an
# entry as 'new'.
#
# This file should SHRINK. Deleting a line here means that file must be
# clean of that finding type. Never add to it by hand — fix the code, or
# regenerate deliberately with --write-baseline and say why in the commit.
#
# 2026-08-25 (llm#1030): 29 -> 35. The rise is a NEW PATTERN, not new debt.
# `swallowed-status-fn` flags a function whose last command discards stderr
# and status while a caller captures its stdout — the llm#1012 shape, which
# patterns 1 and 2 could not see because the swallow and its misreading were
# one function call apart. The 11 instances it found (6 files) were all
# already there; they became visible, not new. Five sit in
# .claude/scripts/roborev_merge_gate.sh, the dry-run predecessor to
# bin/roborev_merge_gate.sh — worth fixing or retiring, since a dry-run gate
# that always exits 0 cannot gate anything either way.
#
# The SHRINK rule stands. This file is now 35 and should head back down.
